// =================================================
// ESP32 SEWING OPERATION COUNTER + RFID CARD READER
// 1.8" ST7735 (160x128) + HW-147C (Si512 / PN512 / MFRC522-compatible)
//
// v3.0.0  IoT CLONE BUILD -- self-provisioning, no pasted key/machine ID
//  - Identity is now the board's own WiFi MAC (hw_id), computed on boot --
//    MACHINE_ID / LOCAL_* / DEVICE_KEY constants are GONE.
//  - On boot: calls POST .../api/v1/device/hello with just its hw_id. An
//    unknown hw_id self-registers as "pending" server-side -- nothing
//    needs to be created in the app first. Once an admin approves it
//    (giving it a Machine ID in the IoT Devices page), the NEXT hello
//    call returns a device_key -- ONE TIME ONLY -- which this firmware
//    saves to flash (Preferences) and uses from then on. If you re-flash
//    or factory-reset the board, it goes back to "pending" until an
//    admin re-approves the same hw_id (the key is only ever handed out
//    once per approval).
//  - Talks to the ISOLATED IOT CLONE, not the live production API --
//    reachable over the public internet via https://ina.technoactive.work/iot-clone/
//    (nginx proxies that path to the clone backend on the server, port
//    8504 -- a completely separate process/DB-write-path from the real
//    production app).
//  - Job resolution replaces the old local N/N_MIN/QTY constants: the
//    server tells this board its style, operation and the computed
//    stitch target (seam length / SPI) for the size it's running, or
//    the smallest-size fallback if the exact size isn't known here.
//    There's no server-side "quantity remaining" concept yet in the IoT
//    clone (unlike the old local-only mode) -- FINISHED/DISCARDED counts
//    below are LOCAL counters only, reset whenever the job (style or
//    operation) changes. The "QTY" box on screen now shows the SIZE the
//    stitch target came from instead (amber if it's the fallback size,
//    not an exact match).
//  - HTTPS via WiFiClientSecure::setInsecure() (no CA bundle needed) --
//    fine for R&D; swap in a proper root CA if this becomes permanent.
//  - All sensor/RFID/display DRAWING logic below is UNCHANGED from the
//    previous build -- only identity + server-sync + a few on-screen
//    labels were touched.
//
// Board: ESP32 Dev Module   Partition: "Default 4MB with spiffs"
// Sketch folder: sewing_counter_rfid/sewing_counter_rfid.ino
//
// TFT_eSPI/User_Setup.h:
//   ST7735_DRIVER, TFT_WIDTH 128, TFT_HEIGHT 160
//   TFT_MOSI 23, TFT_SCLK 26, TFT_CS 5, TFT_DC 16, TFT_RST 17
//   // TFT_MISO 19  <- MUST stay commented out
//   SPI_FREQUENCY 10000000
//   LOAD_GLCD, LOAD_FONT2, LOAD_FONT4, LOAD_GFXFF, SMOOTH_FONT enabled
//
// POWER (recommended)
//   12V adapter -> 1A fuse -> 1N5822 -> 12V rail
//   12V rail -> sensors (brown), PC817 IN1/IN2
//   12V rail -> buck converter set to 5.0V -> ESP32 5V/VIN pin (NOT DC jack)
//   5V rail  -> display VCC (J1 open), 470uF at buck output
//   ESP32 3.3V -> RFID VCC, display LED, 10k pull-ups
//   ONE star ground for everything
//
// WIRING
//  Display: SDA 23  SCK 26  CS 5  A0 16  RESET 17  LED 3.3V  VCC 5V
//  RFID:    SCK 14  MISO 32  MOSI 33  SS 25  VCC 3.3V
//  Fabric:  module V1 -> GPIO 19 (+10k to 3.3V)
//  Stitch:  module V2 -> GPIO 34 (+10k to 3.3V)
// =================================================

